(Notice: Valhalla denies rice export ban reports) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P1] The Valhalla trade ministry denies reports that it plans to restrict rice) Tj
T*
(exports.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P2] No ban, quota or licence requirement is being prepared. Valhalla will) Tj
T*
(continue to export rice to its usual buyers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P3] The reports of 14 and 15 December are wrong. They did not come from the) Tj
T*
(ministry or from any official source.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P4] Valhalla's exportable surplus is small compared with Vanir's. Extra) Tj
T*
(shipments can rise only by about 30 to 35 percent on the current base.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P5] The ministry is monitoring domestic prices and will act if the local market) Tj
T*
(comes under pressure, but no measure is planned now.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P6] The denial follows two days of speculation on social media and in a trade) Tj
T*
(blog, which said a ban was being drafted.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P7] Officials said the ministry had not met exporters to discuss a restriction) Tj
T*
(and had not asked anyone to prepare a notice.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P8] Valhalla's crop is smaller than Vanir's, and most of it is sold under) Tj
T*
(annual contracts rather than on the spot market.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P9] The ministry will publish a short statement if the domestic price position) Tj
T*
(changes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P10] Signed: Ingrid Stahl, trade official, Valhalla.) Tj
T*
() Tj
